# 21. COMPLETE GAP REGISTER

Create a dedicated **KnowledgeOS Theory Gap Register**.

Every gap must be explicit.

Classify gaps into:

### G1 — Definition gap

A concept has no adequate definition.

### G2 — Mathematical derivation gap

A conclusion is stated but derivation is incomplete.

### G3 — Proof gap

A proposition appears plausible but has no proof.

### G4 — Counterexample risk

A proposition may be false and requires falsification.

### G5 — Statistical gap

Statistical assumptions or inference are insufficient.

### G6 — Computational gap

Theory cannot yet be computationally demonstrated.

### G7 — Complexity gap

Computational feasibility is unknown.

### G8 — Evidence gap

The empirical/source evidence is insufficient.

### G9 — Architectural mapping gap

Theory does not map clearly to architecture.

### G10 — Semantic/DDD gap

Domain semantics are ambiguous or inconsistent.

### G11 — Terminology gap

The same term has multiple meanings.

### G12 — Integration gap

Two parts of the theory have not been shown to compose.

### G13 — Empirical validation gap

Theory has not been tested against reality.

### G14 — Formalization gap

Informal reasoning has not yet been converted into formal mathematics.

